"note": "Ambler numbering (the numbering of 2GDN chain A and of the NMR papers; BLAC-J1/J2 numbering_note). Mobile = the active-site segments carrying the apo-CPMG group-fit residues F68, C69, T71, E166, E168, N170, T215, A218 (BLAC-J1) and the broadened S70, S130 (BLAC-J2), plus the segments that show two conformations in the G132N crystal 7A74 (Ser104-Ile105, Ser130, loop 214-216; BLAC-r9 / BLAC-J17): 68-72 (S70 strand-helix junction), 101-107 (S104-I105 loop), 128-133 (SDN loop), 164-180 (Omega loop; 2GDN helix 167-171), 213-221 (214-216 loop and T215/A218). The broadened T235/T237 lie on the core beta3 strand 230-238 and stay in the core. Core = the rest, excluding 144-146 (Ambler insertion 145A-D cannot be represented by an integer auth_seq_id). 'open' = resting wild type 2GDN chain A (BLAC-r15: 'wild-type BlaC modelled from the crystal structure 2GDN'); 'closed' = G132N 7A74 chain A, the only deposited structure whose authors tie its double conformations to a second NMR state (BLAC-r9: 'matching the two states seen by NMR'; it is a mutant, grown with 100 mM phosphate). The authors describe the 7A74 differences as a cis peptide, side chains and the 214-216 loop, so a Calpha comparison is expected to be weakly informative; the inhibitor adducts 3CG5 (clavulanate) and 4DF6 (avibactam) of BLAC-r3 are placed in the table for comparison. PO4 is counted as a ligand because the anion site is the point at issue (BLAC-J2; 5NJ2 is deposited as 'bound to phosphate'). Renumbering: three deposited schemes, mapped to Ambler by Needleman-Wunsch alignment of each chain to 2GDN chain A (<=3 mismatches per chain, all at deposited mutations): (a) UniProt-sequential 3CG5, 3DWZ, 3IQA, 3M6B, 3M6H, 3N6I-3NDG, 3NY4, 4JLF, 4Q8I, 4QB8, 4QHC, 4X6T (auth 43-97 -> -14, 98-157 -> -12, 162-254 -> -16, 255-267 -> -15, 268-307 -> -14; the 145A-D insertion and Ambler gaps 84-85, 239, 253 explain the steps); (b) plain sequential without Ambler gaps: 4DF6, 5NJ2, 5OYO, 6B5X-6B6F, 6H27, 6N14, 7K8E-7K8L, 8EBI-8GCX (29-83 -> 0, 84-143 -> +2, 148-240 -> -2, 241-253 -> -1, 254-293 -> 0; 5NJ2 skips auth 254 so its tail is 255-294 -> -1); (c) 7A5T-7A74, 8BTU-8BTW, 8OE1/8OE5, 9QI5-9QI7 number the first helix one residue low (auth 28-57 -> +1, then 59-293 -> 0, auth 58 absent); 3ZHH keeps Ambler up to 238 then runs sequentially (239-251 -> +1, 252-291 -> +2). 2GDN, 3VFF, 3VFH, 4EBL, 4EBN, 4EBP, 8BV4, 8R88, 8RFZ, 8RG2, 8RII, 9HCK, 9HIT, 9HJ2 are already Ambler."
}
